# Intro

\
Earlier this year, I finally made the decision to upgrade my phone. \
I was upgrading from an iPhone 8 Plus, with 8 plus (get it?) years of continuous use. I had bought the iPhone with my first paycheck from my first job in high school, and for sentimental reasons it was hard to let go. But the battery barely lasted an hour or two, and eventually it was time to upgrade.\
\
I researched for months what phone I should get. From flagship phones like iPhone and Samsung, to crazier phones from Xiaomi and ASUS, I looked at them all. I ended up choosing the Pixel 10 Pro XL, not only because I was a big proponent of Google AI at the time, but because I thought the design was quite sexy and there was a 50% off sale at Visible. \
\
But after over 7 months of usage, I think I'm already ready to trade this phone in. I hope this article can be of some help for people, like me, that are thinking of making the switch to a Pixel, particularly those coming from the Apple ecosystem.

So let's get into it.

# The Good

## Camera

I think the camera on the Pixel 10 Pro XL is incredible. My first few weeks with the phone I was oogling at the sheer quality of the images. While I can't directly compare to other phones' camera features, the Pixel didn't leave me wanting more out of it.

### Pro Zoom

Particularly with the Pixel, they have an AI-enhancer, called Pro Zoom, which enhances images that were taken high zoom (30x or greater). I tested out the 100x Pro Zoom (insane to me that a phone camera even has 100x zoom) at the beach and got incredible results. Here's an example:

**Before**

{% Image
   src="https://cdn.bobbeh.io/articles/5cd150ae-8dde-4560-aeda-051c2a826fc6-pxl_20260320_172639843.burst-02.original.jpg"
   alt="Picture of a boat at 100x zoom, not AI-enhanced with Pro Zoom" /%}

**After**

{% Image
   src="https://cdn.bobbeh.io/articles/12b896bf-0072-44e5-b772-97d38ec3e428-pxl_20260320_172639843.burst-01.jpg"
   alt="Picture of a boat at 100x zoom, enhanced with Google's Pro Zoom feature" /%}

\
While I don't use Pro Zoom a ton, it was still insane to see how high-quality the images can get from the AI-enhancement. It obviously is just an AI-guess as to what the object would look like, but for being a free option to use with the phone I think it's awesome.

### Astrophotography

Another mode of the Pixel 10 Pro XL's camera I used (and still use to this day) is the Astrophotography mode. It essentially is a compilation of long-exposures over a couple minutes. You don't need to adjust any other setting, just set Astrophotography mode and walk away. \
Here are a few pictures I took with the Astrophotography mode enabled:\

{% Image
   src="https://cdn.bobbeh.io/articles/8eab587f-4e81-4a54-8183-38d0a2012c42-pxl_20260513_044644514.night.jpg" /%}

